From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:33:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] MinGW: fix MSVC-only code paths

_WIN32 code that really means MSVC (or the MSVC STL):
- __declspec(align(x)) becomes an unknown, silently ignored attribute in
  GCC: use __attribute__((aligned)) for PADDLE_ALIGN/ALIGN32
- cpuid via <cpuid.h>, no gettimeofday/sleep/pid_t shims, no __m256
  operator+=, Windows API path of CpuUtilization keyed on _WIN32
- MinGW's dirent has no d_type; libstdc++ fstream takes const wchar_t*,
  not std::wstring; do not stream wchar_t* into error messages
- dynload: libwarpctc.dll/libwarprnnt.dll, LAPACK from libopenblas.dll
- float16.h re-#defined __SSE2__ as empty, breaking GCC 16's
  <bits/version.h>; missing <cstdint> includes
